15:     """
16:     Stack alternating original and vertically flipped wave patterns into a taller output.
17: 
18:     Input structure:
19:     - The input is a colored wave pattern on a black background.
20:     - Wave segments touch in a way that overlaps by one row when repeated.
21:     - The output width matches the input width.
22: 
23:     Rule:
24:     - Create an output whose height holds four overlapping copies of the input.
25:     - Flip the input vertically for every other copy.
26:     - Paste original, flipped, original, and flipped patterns with one-row overlaps.
27: 
28:     Key insight:
29:     - Alternating vertical flips continues the wave smoothly because each copy starts
30:       before the previous one fully ends.
31:     """
32:     # Plan:
33:     # 1. Create output grid
34:     # 2. Flip the input grid horizontally and put it in the output repeatedly
